finding: P2 src/engine/runtime/gpu.ts:1404-1407,1424-1432: capturing bundle formats consumes descriptor.fragment.targets before passing the same descriptor to native pipeline creation. GPUFragmentState.targets is an Iterable, not necessarily a reusable array. With a generator yielding {format:"rgba8unorm"}, Array.from exhausts it, so native creation sees no color targets. Independently reproduced in headless Chromium using a minimal createApp initialize hook and a validation scope: CreateRenderPipeline reports "No attachment was specified." Both synchronous and asynchronous paths consume it first, even after the drain when no prime will run. Normalize the target iterable once and give native pipeline creation the same materialized target list used to capture formats. The descriptor-mutation correction otherwise resolves the original finding; the new mutation/null-slot controls use reusable arrays and do not expose this failure.
